^SAMPLE = GSM2914994
!Sample_title = E18.5 kidney 1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM2914994
!Sample_status = Public on Jan 09 2018
!Sample_submission_date = Jan 08 2018
!Sample_last_update_date = Jan 24 2018
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Developing mouse kidney
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Developing mouse kidney
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = strain: C57BL/6
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Kidney organoids were made according to a published protocol (Takasata et al., Generation of kidney organoids from human pluripotent stem cells, Nature protocols 2016, PMID:27560173.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Mouse kidneys were dissected into ice cold PBS then digested over 15 minutes at 37C in Accutase, with manual dissociation via pippetting through a P1000 tip every 5 minutes. Following dissociation, cells were passed through a 30 micron filter and stored on ice in 50% PBS, 50% DMEM with 10% FCS. Human kidney organoids were dissociated via a similar protocol using Trypsin instead of Accutase and stored on ice in APEL media.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Chromium Single Cell Library kit V2
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Illumina HiSeq HT chemistry- 100bp paired end sequencing
!Sample_description = kidney_counts.csv.gz
!Sample_data_processing = The 10x Genomics Cell Ranger pipeline (v1.3.1) was used to align, filter and de-duplicate reads before counting those overlapping genes to produce count matrices for each sample.
!Sample_data_processing = Count matrics from the kidney samples were combined using cellranger aggr with no normalisation, as were those from the organoid samples. The resulting datasets consist of matrix files (kid_matrix.mtx, org_matrix.mtx) containing the UMI count values, barcode files (kid_barcodes.tsv, org_matrix.tsv) containing the detected cell barcodes and genes files (kid_genes.tsv, org_genes.tsv) containing the ENSEMBL ids of the detected genes. These have been converted to dense matrices in CSV format (kidney_counts.csv, org_counts.csv).
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10 / hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: CSV files containing raw count matrices.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL17021
!Sample_contact_name = Luke,,Zappia
!Sample_contact_institute = Murdoch Childrens Research Institute
!Sample_contact_address = 50 Flemington Road
!Sample_contact_city = Parkville
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 3052
!Sample_contact_country = Australia
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina HiSeq 2500
!Sample_library_selection = cDNA
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN08325525
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX3583354
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE
!Sample_series_id = GSE108291
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
